      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>Richard Collis’s English translation of Aleinu with Al Kein and Al Tira is provided in the liner notes for tracks 61 and 62 of his album <tei:hi rend="italic">We Sing We Stay Together: Shabbat Morning Service Prayers</tei:hi> (2019).</tei:p>
        <tei:p>Aleinu, authored sometime in Antiquity, first appears in the liturgy for the Yom Kippur musaf service. It also is found in a first person variation among the hymns in the hekhalot texts. Aleinu became a familiar prayer for concluding services only after the beginning of the terrible massacres that befell the Jews of Ashkenaz during the Crusades. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
